1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,750
Jump Game — LeetCode 55

2
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:04,600
Problem: nums[i] is the max jump length from index i. Starting at index 0, can you reach the last index?

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,600
Example: nums = [3, 2, 1, 0, 4] — from index 0 you can jump up to 3

4
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:10,300
Index 4 is the goal — can we get there?

5
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:14,950
Hint: forget how to jump — just track the farthest index you can reach; if you ever stand beyond it, you're stuck

6
00:00:14,950 --> 00:00:19,850
Approach: greedy — keep maxReach; at each i, maxReach = max(maxReach, i + nums[i]); i > maxReach means false, reaching the end means true

7
00:00:19,850 --> 00:00:24,700
Start: maxReach = 0, only index 0 is reachable

8
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:27,440
i = 0 is within reach; jump 3 → reach extends to index 3

9
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:29,580
i = 1: 1 + 2 = 3, no farther

10
00:00:29,580 --> 00:00:31,720
i = 2: 2 + 1 = 3, no farther

11
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:34,010
i = 3: 3 + 0 = 3 — the zero is a dead stop

12
00:00:34,010 --> 00:00:36,900
i = 4 is beyond the reach of 3 → stuck, return false

13
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:39,840
The 0 at index 3 is the wall — the reach stalls at 3

14
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:43,390
Make it a 1 and you'd reach the end. Time O(n), space O(1)

15
00:00:43,390 --> 00:00:48,500
